  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1: Rain showers, drizzle, and cooler temperatures will \ncontinue into Thursday. Drier and more seasonable temperatures \nreturn for the weekend and persist into next week.\n\nCool wedging pattern continues into Thursday, featuring areas of\nlight rain, drizzle, and patchy fog. Cool, below normal \ntemperatures in the 50s will also persist into Thursday. Rain\nrates today should be light enough to prevent any flooding\nconcerns...in reality, rain today will be beneficial. Coverage\nof rain will diminish through Thursday morning, but clouds\nshould remain most of the day. \n\nWill begin to transition to drier weather on Friday as flow\nturns more northwesterly and a drier airmass filters into the\nregion. This will feature Fall- like, close to normal \ntemperatures into early next week. A few mornings could feature\nlow 40s across the mountains and perhaps a few upper 30s in \nsheltered valleys.",
